==Old English==

===Etymology 1===
From {{proto|Germanic|íχwa-z/-n, *i(g)wá-z/-n|horse|lang=ang}}, from {{proto|Indo-European|h₁éḱwos|horse|lang=ang}}. Cognate with {{osx}} {{l|osx|ehuskalk|''ehu''skalk|lang=osx}} "horse-rider", Old High German [[eha-]] (in personal names), Old Norse [[jór]].  The Indo-European root is also the source of Latin [[equus]], Avestan ''aspa-'', Armenian {{term|էշ||donkey|tr=ēš|lang=hy}}, Tocharian A ''yuk'' B ''yakwe'', {{proto|Baltic|ečwā-|lang=}} (Lithuanian [[ašva|ašvà]]), Old Irish [[ech]] (Irish [[each]]).

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|/eox/|lang=ang}}

====Noun====
{{infl|ang|eoh|g=m, n}}

# {{poetic|lang=ang}} [[horse]], [[steed]]

